Preferred Knowledge/Skills
Demonstrates extensive knowledge and/or a proven record of success in the following areas:
Demonstrating 10+ years of overall experience in software testing that includes testing various TDM implementation and 7 years' experience as a test manager;
Understanding of Agile and Waterfall methodologies;
Working on projects in an international environment;
Working experience in test effort estimates;
Understanding on healthcare, energy and utilities domain;
Working on DBs Oracle, SQL Server, DB2, Postgres, Redshift, MongoDB;
Understanding in managing and using Informatica TDM test data management;
Working on scripting languages like Python and PowerShell to perform the automation around data generation and data validation;
Working in test data management functions like test data generation, test data masking and subsetting;
Working in handling various PII/PHI related regulation through TDM;
Working experience on multiple TDM tools - Delphix, Informatica, IBM Optim;
Working experience in test strategy and tests plans definition (for complex integrated solutions);
Working experience in the use of test management tools e.g. ALM, qTest, JIRA, Azure DevOps etc.;
Working experience in non-functional testing management;
Designing and driving implementation of end-to-end testing strategies and frameworks needed to test all the dimensions of an application platform, including functional correctness, performance, scale, and security across the project/program covering all the workstreams/tracks.;
Managing testing activities for different types of testing - functional, integration, system, regression, performance, security, E2E and UAT support;
Performing analysis, estimation, design, development, testing, implementation of data archiving /test data management/ data privacy solutions;
Developing & executing long term enterprise test data management strategy;
Coordinating activities across multiple operations teams including storage, OS, and DBA teams;
Providing required test data for performance test, user acceptance test, QA test, application development, and other non-production environments;
Providing a consistent and repeatable process to support multiple applications including identifying data elements for masking in applications, data reset and update process;
Working directly with IT security and compliance to ensure policies were consistently followed;
Performing capacity planning / infrastructure to implement a scalable TDM solution;
Interacting with stakeholders to define enterprise level TDM architecture;
Recommending tool and priority for TDM implementation;
Performing evaluation, analysis and makes recommendations regarding tool usage and selection;
Designing and developing test tools that allow teams to scale out to support new features;
Providing technical direction and support to team members in multiple geographic locations on testing approach and all aspects of automation testing to ensure industry standards and best practices are followed;
Utilizing tools and methodologies to improve individual team effectiveness and to increase efficiencies in the QA process; and,
Establishing test data management strategies and implementing them for different testing.
