About Orica
At Orica, it’s the power of our people that leads change and shapes our futures. Every day, all around the world, our people help mobilise vital resources essential to progress. Established in 1874, we have grown to become the world leader in mining and civil blasting with a diverse of team of more than 13,000 across the world.
It’s an exciting time to join us – we are shaping the future of mining through digital and automated technologies, embracing new ways of thinking, pioneering innovation and reimagining the way we work.
About the role
We are excited to offer an exceptional opportunity for a talented
Geoscience Data Administrator
to join our prestigious Geophysics team at Orica. As a renowned global industry leader, we are committed to responsible operations, prioritizing safety, and minimizing our environmental footprint.
As a
Geoscience Data Administrator
, you will be a vital contributor to our team, specializing in geoscience data management. Your role will involve supporting data acquisition, quality assurance/quality control (QA/QC), storage, and management of geoscience datasets. Your expertise will ensure that our customers derive maximum value from Orica products.
At Orica, we value innovation and collaboration. As part of our Geophysics team, you will have the opportunity to work with cutting-edge technologies and collaborate with industry experts. We provide a supportive and inclusive work environment that fosters growth and development.
What you will be doing
Acquire geoscience datasets from various sources, including field surveys, sensors, and external databases;
Develop and implement efficient processes for data extraction, transformation, and loading (ETL) into the data management program;
Establish and execute QA/QC procedures to ensure the accuracy, completeness, and reliability of geoscience data;
Collaborate with geoscientists and other stakeholders to validate data integrity and resolve discrepancies;
Design and implement a robust data storage infrastructure that aligns with industry best practices and compliance standards;
Manage data repositories and ensure proper organization and indexing for easy retrieval;
Develop and maintain metadata standards for geoscience datasets;
Establish and enforce data management policies, procedures, and best practices;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand data requirements and optimize data workflows;
Administer the data management program, ensuring optimal performance, security, and reliability;
Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues related to data storage and access.
What you will bring
Bachelor's degree in a relevant field such as geoscience, data science, or information management;
Proven experience as a Data Administrator or similar role, preferably in the mining or geoscience industry;
Strong understanding of geoscience data types, formats, and industry-specific challenges;
Proficiency in data management programs and tools, with experience in system administration;
Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills with a keen attention to detail;
Familiarity with relevant regulations and compliance standards in the mining industry.
What we offer
As part of a truly global company, you will have the ability to grow and learn in a diverse, collaborative culture. We foster relationships and learning through connected global and local teams, promote flexible and diverse career paths and support the development of your knowledge and skills.
You will be paid a competitive salary, learn from talented individuals across multiple disciplines and be able to thrive in a safe workplace within a collaborative culture. Ignite your career at a place where your distinct potential can find its home.
We respect and value all
Orica promotes and fosters a culture of inclusion and Equal Opportunity Employment everywhere we operate. We treat our people and applicants with fairness, dignity, and respect, getting the best of everyone’s contributions.
All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, nationality, age, military or veteran, marital or disability status.
