Banyan Software provides the best permanent home for successful enterprise software companies, their employees, and customers. We are on a mission to acquire, build and grow great enterprise software businesses all over the world that have dominant positions in niche vertical markets. In recent years, Banyan was named the #1 fastest-growing private software company in the US on the Inc. 5000 and amongst the top 10 fastest-growing companies by the Deloitte Technology Fast 500. Founded in 2016 with a permanent capital base setup to preserve the legacy of founders, Banyan focuses on a buy and hold for life strategy for growing software companies that serve specialized vertical markets.
Job Profile
Sourcing acquisitions and engaging business owners is a critical function to the success of our business. We are building a world class sourcing engine to identify, engage, nurture and close acquisitions of great software businesses. In this high-impact role, you will execute priority initiatives on the Tech & Data roadmap, with a focus on enhancing our existing Salesforce platform and delivering complex data-driven initiatives. Leveraging your technical prowess and analytical skillset, you will establish yourself as our resident data SME and continuously seek to better understand and evolve our data and related CRM processes, all geared towards supercharging our sales/marketing efforts and sourcing more acquisitions. This is a tremendous opportunity to join a fast-growing company with a start-up mentality where innovative thinking is encouraged. If you love working with Salesforce, have a passion for solving complex problems and building solutions with an amazing team, please join us!
Responsibilities
Salesforce Administration: Support overall Sales Cloud configuration, maintenance and enhancements to ensure optimal performance and functionality.
Data Management & Delivery: Support data integrity, quality and governance objectives, while collaborating with users to understand requirements and execute initiatives on our data roadmap.
Data Analysis: Apply advanced data analysis techniques to derive meaningful insights from applications across our technology stack, ultimately leveraging these findings to inform strategic decisions and identify opportunities for process improvement and innovation.
KPIs & Reporting: Implement and enhance tracking and reporting mechanisms to monitor individual, team and organizational KPIs.
Operations and Support: Investigate and analyze reported issues and bugs, diagnosing root causes and proposing solutions. Develop and implement fixes and enhancements, adhering to best practices and industry standards.
Divine Discontent: Continuously explore new technologies and ways of doing things; we are on a mission to be best-in-class and proposing innovative solutions is encouraged.
Qualifications For Success
Salesforce Administrator certification is required; additional certifications are a plus;
Proven Salesforce work experience, inclusive of configuration, customization and data management;
Strong analytical skills, with the ability to translate data into actionable insights for strategy;
Advanced Salesforce reporting skills, such as matrix reports, cross filters, reporting formulas, etc. SQL/SOQL is a plus;
Experience with BI tools (Looker, Tableau) and knowledge of visualization best practices preferred;
Familiarity with supplementary and integrated CRM sales technologies, including account-based marketing, sales engagement, lead generation and revenue intelligence platforms;
Highly motivated, with an extreme willingness to learn and up-skill;
Ability to think and work independently and as part of a team;
A love of technology as a tool for solving company problems, as well as a knack for self-initiated research and process improvement;
A related post-secondary degree is preferred (i.e. computer science, business management, data science, applied mathematics or statistics, etc.)
Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Equal Employment Opportunity at Banyan: Banyan affirms that inequality is detrimental to our Teams, associates, our Operating Companies, and the communities we serve. Our goal is to impact lasting change through our actions. Together, we unite for equality and equity. Banyan is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of any protected characteristic, including race, color, genetic information, creed, national origin, religion, sex, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, lawful alien status, ancestry, age, marital status, or protected veteran status and will not discriminate against anyone on the basis of a disability. We support an inclusive workplace where associates excel based on personal merit, qualifications, experience, ability, and job performance.
