RWE Trading Americas Inc.
To start as soon as possible, full time / part time, permanent
Your future plans
RWE Trading Americas Inc. ("RWETA") is a dynamic energy trading company based in the heart of New York City. As a wholly owned subsidiary of RWE Supply & Trading GmbH, the globally active commercial hub of international renewable energy company RWE AG, RWETA boasts an extensive cross-commodity trading and origination mandate and access to world class energy trading infrastructure and expertise.
The energy transition continues to disrupt regional commodity markets and with the Americas being a core growth region for the RWE group, RWETA has ambitious expansion plans and seeks highly motivated and experienced professionals to join the NYC-based team.
This is a unique career opportunity to play a key role in the formation of a trading and origination business in a market of strategic importance to a long established, and highly respected international energy trading company that has physical and financial energy markets in its DNA.
As the objective is to increase the profitability and efficiency of our trading business, you are an integral part of RWETA’s commercial team, reporting directly to the Head of Americas Trading and Origination;
As our local expert interface for all things ‘trading data analytics’, you will familiarise yourself with the existing and available front office IT systems, processes, and data sources in order to lead the processing and presentation of large datasets, ranging from commodity trading and time series data through the many drivers of regional energy supply and demand;
Working alongside front office colleagues, and in collaboration with relevant teams across the global organization to ensure consistent inputs and approach, you will design and implement effective and intuitive analytics solutions tailored to RWETA’s specific trading desk requirements, constantly evolving as market and product coverage expand;
Upon gaining significant exposure to the exciting North American energy sector, you will embrace the opportunity to develop statistical and machine learning models, and constantly explore new and creative ways to present insights and patterns to inform trading decisions;
Your Powerful Skills
You hold a Master’s degree in computer science, mathematics or related field, and have at least 3 years’ experience in a data driven environment as an applied data scientist/engineer/quant, ideally in a trading environment;
In depth knowledge of relevant programming languages such as Python, R, SQL, and a proven track record building and deploying data mining algorithms and performing statistical analysis on large datasets;
Preferably you are familiar with Tableau and other data visualization tools, and demonstrate a passion for effectively transforming raw data into exciting and actionable insights;
Interest in learning more about the wholesale energy commodity markets and the fundamentals behind the data;
You have excellent analytics presentation and communication skills and are enthusiastic about interaction with commercial and support function teams, including regular interaction across a global organization;
Ability to creatively apply data and analytics technology to solve commercial problems;
Self-motivated, a strong team player, but confident working autonomously to deliver complex projects and multiple tasks with a high attention to detail within a fast-paced environment;
You are excited to work in a role requiring daily in-person collaboration with your colleagues on our state-of-the-art trading floor in central Manhattan.
What we value most is passion, willingness to learn and a determined and resilient work ethic. So, even if you think you do not yet display all of the skills above we would still like to hear from you.
Further we welcome applications from individuals who may not be able to commit to full-time roles. At RWEST, finding the right person for the job is our top priority, and we are willing to explore flexible arrangements.
Our offer
We offer an environment where working is meaningful, respected and supported. There are also a few things more that you will experience:
RWE Supply & Trading is a leading European energy trading company and top tier global employer. Our incredibly diverse and dedicated team of experts has been representing the RWE Group on the global wholesale markets for energy and energy-related raw materials and services for more than 20 years. Building on the continuous evolution of our European trading footprint, and the successful expansion of our local trading presence in the APAC region, we now have a strong confidence and commitment to succeed with our growth plans in North America;
We offer competitive terms of employment, excellent benefits, and an open and collaborative work environment.
rwe.com/career
Apply now with just a few clicks: ad code
84234,
Any questions? Madlen Krembel, M: +49-162-2960416 (Recruiting)
We look forward to meeting you!
We value diversity and therefore welcome all applications, irrespective of gender, disability, nationality, ethnic and social background, religion and beliefs, age or sexual orientation and identity. #inclusionmatters
Of course, you can find us on LinkedIn, Twitter and Xing, too.
RWE Supply & Trading is the interface between RWE and the energy markets around the world. Around 2,000 employees from over 70 different countries trade electricity, gas, commodities and CO2 emission allowances. The trading entity also ensures the commercial optimisation of RWE’s power plant dispatch and markets electricity from RWE.
